    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e1",
      "title": "The French r",
      "body": "The French r is not made with the tongue tip like in English. It is made in the back of the throat, a soft friction, a little like clearing your throat very gently or a quiet gargle."
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e2",
      "title": "How to find it",
      "body": "• Say a long ah. Now say g-g-g-ah. Feel the back of your tongue touch the soft palate.\n• Say ha, then make the h rough and soft in the throat: hRa.\n• Keep the tongue tip down, touching your bottom front teeth, and do not move it."
    },
