    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e3",
      "title": "In Canada",
      "body": "The r varies a lot in Québec: it can be more rolled or more relaxed depending on the region. A clear standard r is enough for the exam. Do not worry about getting it perfect on day one."
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e4",
      "title": "Speaking: R practice",
      "body": "Say slowly, then faster: rue, rouge, merci, par, bonjour, regarder. Say Bonjour, merci, au revoir three times. Record yourself.\n\n• If your r sounds like an English r, relax your tongue and keep the tip against your bottom teeth.\n• Do not push. Soft and in the throat is better than hard."
    },
